  "strategy": "### Approach and Rationale:\nI propose using a hybrid global-local search algorithm that represents functions as point distributions and optimizes correlations simultaneously. This approach:\n\n1. **Global Search**: Uses simulated annealing to explore diverse structures at multiple resolutions (95, 190, 285, 380)\n2. **Local Refinement**: Employs coordinate ascent to sharpen promising configurations\n3. **Resolution Transfer**: Gradually increases resolution while preserving key probability mass concentrations\n\nThe bottleneck of previous approaches was local optima trapping. This method combines global exploration over shape spaces with targeted optimization of correlation metrics, which should yield better structural avoidance.\n\nKey innovations:\n1. Probability-constrained random patches to preserve diversity\n2. Dynamic resolution splits based on feature density\n3. Progressive gradient projection to enforce constraints\n\n### Mathematical Specification:\n**Variables**: Probability mass distribution \\(p(\\boldsymbol{x})\\) over domain \\(D = [0,2]\\) with \\( \\int_D p(\\boldsymbol{x})d\\boldsymbol{x} = 1 \\)\n\n**Objective**: Minimize \\(C_4 = \\max_k \\int_D p(\\boldsymbol{x})(1-p(\\boldsymbol{x+k}))d\\boldsymbol{x}\\)\n\n**Representation**: Piecewise constant at N points (232 points by default)\n\n**Constraints**:\n- Normalization: \\( \\sum p_i / N = 1 \\)\n- Non-negativity: \\( p_i \\ge 0 \\)\n- Space constraints: \\( ||\\nabla p_i||_1 \\le \\eta \\)\n\n**Convexification**: We approximate the discrete correlation as:\n- \\( C_4 \\approx \\max_k \\|p \\circledast q_k\\|_1 \\)\n\nFeatures:\n- Breaks supremum search into coordinate-aligned passes\n- Uses Toeplitz matrix factorization for correlation\n- Exploits separability of indicators\n\n### Implementation Procedure:\n**Setup**:\n1. Initialize uniformly at random \\(N\\) points: \\( \\{ \\mathbf{x}_i \\}_{i=1}^N \\)\n2. Define projection operator:\n   ```\n   def project_feasible(x):\n       x = np.clip(x, 0, 1)\n       diff = sum(x) * 2/N - 1\n       if abs(diff) > 1e-4:\n           # Magnitude adjustment\n           x = x * (1/(1+diff/float(1)))\n       return x\n   ```\n3. Main optimization loop:\n   ```\n   best_c = float('inf')\n   for resolution in [232, 400, ...]:    # adaptive doubling\n       points = [2*i/(resolution-1) for i in range(resolution)]   # uniform grid\n       p = feasible_init(resolution)  # np.random.rand(resolution)/1.5\n       while time_remaining():\n           # Simulated annealing for global search\n           new_p = perturb(p)\n           try:\n               new_c = compute_correlation(new_p)\n               if new_c < best_c or random.random() < (1 - tic()):\n                   p = new_p\n                   best_c = new_c\n           except:\n               continue\n           # Local gradient-based\n           grad = compute_gradient(p)\n           p -= alpha * grad\n           p = project_feasible(p)\n   ```\n\n**Local Search**:\n1. Gradient computation:\n   ```\n   def compute_gradient(p):\n       dx = 2/N   # step size\n       g = np.zeros_like(p)\n       for i in range(len(p)):\n           # Central difference for most points\n           # requires loop over positions, being careful at boundaries\n           ...\n   ```\n2. Local projection:\n   ```\n   def local_optimize(p):\n       # all-constraint version using iterative clipping\n       for _ in range(5):\n           if sum(p) * 2/N - 1 < -1e-4:\n               # inject mass where low\n           else:\n               # siphon mass from high areas (1-STOP)\n           # Clip to [0,1]\n   ```\n\n**Convolution Mutations**:\n1. Add structured noise:\n   ```\n   def perturb(p):\n       sigma = 0.05   # standard deviation\n       r0 = random.randint(0, len(p))\n       sizes = random.randint(5, 20)\n       patch = norm.pdf(np.arange(-sizes, sizes) / sigma) * 0.1\n       p[r0:r0+sizes] += patch[:len(p[r0:r0+sizes])]\n       return scale_to_feasible(p)\n   ```\n\n### Search Choices:\n1. **Initial Conditions**: Uniform random field at n=232 points\n2. **Perturbation Schedule**:\n   - Start with random walks (100 steps)\n   - Then targeted gradient updates (1000 steps)\n3. **Restart Policy**:\n   - Change patch injection strategy every 500 evaluations\n   - Dynamic resolution switch if improvement stalls\n\n### Budget Projection:\n- N=232 requires ~100ms per candidate\n- Gradient computation ~50ms\n- 5e6 candidates would take ~500 seconds\n- Optimize by:\n  - Early termination at local minima\n  - Progressive candidate density reduction\n\n### Validation and Final Returns:\n**Feasibility checks**:\n- Explicit bounds: -2 < x_i < 2\n- Normalization: |sum x_i - expected| < 0.5 (at resolution 232)\n- Objective bounds: C_4 must fit within machine precision\n\n**Output preparation**:\n1. Always return best_c\n2. Format as: `(best_p, best_c, n_232_points)`\n3. Preserve evaluation continuity\n\nThis strategy provides structured but adaptive search, with clear mathematical foundation. The key is structured exploration at meaningful scales while respecting application constraints.",
